        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_922dd91f243141308ac94e70445a933a",
      "statement": "For Doze resilience (v2.6.11) the poller acquires a partial wake lock (Messages:OutboxPoller) for exactly the in-flight part of each cycle — long-poll + delivery + ack — and releases it in a finally block before the ~5s idle/error gap, so the device sleeps normally between cycles and battery cost is proportional to bridge duty rather than wall-clock time.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/OutboxPoller.kt#L110-L122",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a14e76d9890712ad0ffaee829e8f8942ffd78a76a83ba6460c9e509bf317556e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/OutboxPoller.kt#L55-L85",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5645686b4698facf631816d975685be7c6f6f8f4513137229092bf1114a4e8a8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bd03fedac64a4e4dbd5b4fe42708dd9e",
      "statement": "The wake lock is acquired with a 90s timeout that acts as the anti-leak safety net (normal release happens in finally); without the lock the in-flight long-poll socket dies silently in Doze, the server sees no device polling and refuses sends, and every Eve send fails with 503 android_gateway_unreachable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml#L23-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:49ec0af1d78b13ea029af5ace8c80aa656efe3b7ef63dd666b96a3316dbfe1f5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/src/main/java/com/autonomousone/messages/gateway/OutboxPoller.kt#L72-L85",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36ecc1897e5b28fc3f0ae08a6839d622a95ab004871a35dca58b1425b4e26bad:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/release-v2.6.11.md#L5-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cba1bce0aa80ebad7a3077a68cc1d447fbe896e9a6777f7d5ff12f0802a3f33c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7922f894003a435ea969a36230820d17",
      "statement": "The per-cycle wake lock is complemented by service-level Doze protections: the WAKE_LOCK and FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC permissions, an honest dataSync|specialUse foreground-service type declared in the manifest and set at startForeground, and a setExactAndAllowWhileIdle watchdog that re-fires ACTION_START on service death — together keeping the pull loop alive.",
      "evidence": [
